// A FUNCTION IS NOT A SORT — the `func` counterpart of `sorts_reject_callable_as_sort.b4m`.
//
// `f` has a signature (`Elem => Elem`); the APPLICATION `f(x)` has a sort, `f` does not. There
// is no function-type sort to quantify over, which is the same first-order restriction that
// stops `forall p: Prop;` — nothing higher-order is nameable in a binder.
sort Elem
func f(x: Elem) => Elem

theorem aFuncIsNotASort: forall p: f; p = p
proof
  @conclusion |
    forall p: f; p = p
    [by reflexivity]
qed
